`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"The attention variant sets the size of the key-value (KV) cache. The KV cache is a per-sequence store that inference uses. It holds a key vector and a value vector for every past token. Weeks 3 and 4 build three attention variants: multi-head attention (MHA), grouped-query attention (GQA) and multi-head latent attention (MLA)."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Mixture-of-experts (MoE) models need extra techniques for stability during post-training."}),`
